      "notes": "Built by tools/calibrate_mci.py from pseudoreflectance_v4, twelve recordings (v3's eleven plus 2026-06-07-17-13-40, added because rain on a different street rested on two bags and is the arm that transfers worst; chosen by comparing odometry, 97 per cent of its route is road the other two do not cover). I_MCI = kappa*rho after Laasch et al. 2025 - not a reflectance. g(R) SHARED across bags, equal-population bins, bin means, isotonic fit, band 20-60 m. FIVE MEASURED CLASSES. sidewalk is measured here for the first time: v3 carried 0.30 over from v1, 0.55 times asphalt, and the measurement gives 0.6529, 1.19 times asphalt - a factor of two, on 16.8 per cent of the returns the agent receives. Segmenting it needed a second prompt set: the first returned the carriageway, because 'pavement' means the road surface in American usage. unknown is NOT measured and is declared so in measured_materials: the operator leaves those returns as the simulator produced them. A pedestrian class was attempted and abandoned - prompted segmentation put a person on 1452 frames at 0.03 to 0.14 per cent of the image, and an independent detector confirmed 9 per cent of them, which is not agreement enough to support a coefficient. Snow ratios are carried over and unmeasured.",
